## Summary

I've completed spec-driven planning for **Ghost from the Past** by creating seven authoritative files in `.kiro/`:

1. **`.kiro/steering/product.md`** — Product vision, users, privacy promise, and non-goals (no central server, no Chrome Web Store, free tier only).

2. **`.kiro/steering/tech.md`** — Technology stack and conventions: MV3 extension in plain ES2022 with UMD libs (Readability, Turndown), Worker in TypeScript with D1/Vectorize/Workers AI graceful degradation, MCP SDK stateless per-request transport, testing commands, security rules (never log secrets, timingSafeEqual auth, never commit .dev.vars).

3. **`.kiro/steering/design-language.md`** — Visual & interaction design: off-white/black palette (no colour accents), squircle shapes (14px, 999px pills, 12px buttons), system sans-serif stack, 4px grid spacing, bedsheet ghost icon, accessibility standards, friendly-spooky tone.

4. **`.kiro/specs/ghost-from-the-past/requirements.md`** — 22 numbered requirement groups covering capture (R1–R3), queue/sync (R4–R7), popup/options (R8–R10), worker ingest (R11–R16), MCP server (R17–R18), CORS (R19), testing (R20), deployment (R21–R22), all in EARS-style ("WHEN … THEN …") format.

5. **`.kiro/specs/ghost-from-the-past/design.md`** — System architecture diagram (browser → Worker → D1/Vectorize/Workers AI), component & module list with function signatures, D1 schema with indexes, API message formats (ingest request/response, MCP tool JSON), error handling, security/privacy design, testing strategy, correctness properties.

6. **`.kiro/specs/ghost-from-the-past/tasks.md`** — 10-phase implementation plan with ~40 subtasks (scaffold → worker libs → storage → ingest/search → MCP → extension libs → content/background → UI → icons → e2e/docs), each referencing requirement IDs and building sequentially.

7. **`.kiro/hooks/test-on-save.json`** and **`.kiro/hooks/secret-guard.json`** with **`.kiro/hooks/secret-guard.mjs`** — Automated test running on TypeScript/JS saves and pre-commit secret scanning (GHOST_SECRET, Bearer tokens, CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, .dev.vars patterns).

All files follow the brief precisely: independent extension/ and worker/ (no root workspaces), free-tier constraints (5M vector dims ≈ 13k chunks), graceful degradation, MCP Streamable HTTP transport, timeinsafe comparison, no analytics, and .kiro/ always included. The spec is concrete, focused, and ready for implementation.
